WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.850
One of the most wicked teachers in the history
of Hogwarts, Dolores Umbridge is a fascinating

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.960
villain and the woman who played her, Imelda
Staunton, is a versatile and talented performer.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.580
But what happened to the actress after leaving
the franchise?

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.160
Here’s what Staunton has been up to since
Harry Potter.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.060
Imelda Staunton didn't join the Harry Potter
films until the fifth installment, The Order

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.199
of the Phoenix, but she was the perfect choice
to play the multi-layered character of Dolores

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:24.820
Umbridge.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.780
As the new Defense Against the Dark Arts instructor,
the saccharine, pink-clad professor is only

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:32.150
there to dissuade students from actually learning.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.460
This forces Harry and his friends to create
an illegal study group so they can teach themselves

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.460
defensive spells.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.220
If that wasn't bad enough, Umbridge also tortures
her students and, in one scene, she even gets

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.880
a little slap-happy with Harry.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.540
Despite the fact that she's driven out of
Hogwarts by the end of Harry's fifth year,

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.800
Umbridge reappears during the second to last
installment of the film series, Harry Potter

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.480
and the Deathly Hallows, Part One.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:59.260
In classic Umbridge style, she's back to her
old ways of abusing power.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.220
Fortunately, Harry manages to disguise himself
and best her once again.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.600
With a mix of wholesomeness, arrogance, and
cruelty, Staunton's pitch-perfect performance

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.120
as Umbridge left an unforgettable mark on
the series.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.100
After her run in the Harry Potter movies,
it seemed logical for Staunton to transition

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:19.830
into other blockbuster films, and eventually,
she found her way into a few hugely successful

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:20.880
Disney projects.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:26.040
In 2010, Staunton joined Tim Burton's adaptation
of Lewis Carroll's classic novel Alice in

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:26.580
Wonderland.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:31.360
The film even features a few of Staunton's
Harry Potter co-stars, including Alan Rickman,

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.740
Timothy Spall, and Helena Bonham Carter, as
well as Staunton's husband, Jim Carter.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:40.580
She only has a few, short lines as the Talking
Flowers, but Staunton gives her thorny characters

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.120
some serious personality and she comes out...smelling
like a rose.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:44.800
"Stop that."

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.620
Staunton also appeared in Disney's 2014 antihero
tale Maleficent, which stars Angelina Jolie

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.600
as the seemingly evil witch who cursed Aurora,
better known as "Sleeping Beauty."

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.680
Staunton plays a character named Knotgrass.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.480
She's one of three pixies who take human form
and stay by Aurora's side until she becomes

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:02.960
safe from Maleficent's clutches.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:07.900
Staunton later reprised the role in the 2019
sequel Maleficent: Mistress of Evil.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.400
Staunton might not have physically appeared
on screen in her next big project but her

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.960
role was an incredibly vital one.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.880
In 2014's Paddington, Staunton provided the
voice of Aunt Lucy, who remains off-screen

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.490
for most of the film but still manages to
give an emotional backbone to the entire narrative.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:28.490
Paddington spends his childhood with his loving
Aunt Lucy and Uncle Pastuzo, who was voiced

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:29.540
by Michael Gambon.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.440
You might remember him as the actor who played
Albus Dumbledore opposite Staunton.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.740
After Pastuzo tragically dies, Aunt Lucy sends
Paddington to live in London, where he's adopted

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.950
by the quirky and kind Brown family.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.400
In Paddington 2, the little bear embarks on
a mission to bring Aunt Lucy to London to

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.600
live with him and the Browns.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:51.570
Despite many struggles, he eventually succeeds,
and Staunton briefly reprises her role for

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.520
some of the film's most heartfelt moments.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.000
The same year that Staunton made her first
appearance in the Paddington series, she took

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.940
on an emotionally charged and resonant project
called Pride.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.360
The film, based on a true story, is about
a faction of London's LGBTQ+ community that

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.520
bands together to support miners during the
1984 British miner's strike.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:15.940
Though the two groups seem to have very little
in common, the LGBTQ+ community raises money

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:20.630
for the miners, creating a campaign known
as Lesbians and Gays Support the Miners.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.301
Staunton played real-life activist Hefina
Headon, who was part of the Women's Support

00:03:24.301 --> 00:03:25.660
Group and strike committee.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.819
Throughout the film, there's no denying that
Staunton gave a truly powerful performance.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.540
"You better shut her mouth, or I'm gonna do
it permanently."

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:37.800
Staunton earned a BAFTA nomination for Best
Supporting Actress, and the film itself got

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.250
a nod at the Golden Globes for Best Motion
Picture in the Comedy or Musical category.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:47.330
Plus, Pride featured Staunton acting alongside
yet another Harry Potter veteran, Bill Nighy,

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.520
who appeared in The Deathly Hallows, Part
One.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:54.120
After years on the big screen, Staunton took
on some television roles, but true to form

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:58.280
for the talented actress, she wisely chose
high-profile projects that brought her even

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:58.840
more acclaim.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:04.760
In 2007 and 2009, Staunton appeared in Cranford
and its sequel Return to Cranford.

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:08.910
The story of a small town where widows and
unmarried women lead happy, fulfilled lives

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:12.930
within their community, Cranford featured
Staunton as Octavia Pole, one of the more

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.730
gossipy residents of the town.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.719
She was joined on the show by her husband,
Jim Carter, and, once again, her old Harry

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.400
Potter cohort, Michael Gambon.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:26.050
The year 2012 brought Staunton even more critical
success with HBO's original film The Girl,

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:30.180
which told the dark, lurid story of Alfred
Hitchcock and his enduring obsession with

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.440
the leading lady of The Birds, Tippi Hedren.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:37.060
Staunton played Alma Reville, Hitchcock's
long-suffering wife and screenwriting partner.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:41.300
Her performance earned her nominations for
another BAFTA and a Primetime Emmy Award.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.699
After the success of the original series,
it seemed inevitable that Downton Abbey would

00:04:46.699 --> 00:04:51.550
get its own movie, and in 2019, the long-rumored
film finally hit theaters.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.820
It focuses on a visit from King George V to
the Crawley estate.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:00.240
Imelda Staunton's husband, Jim Carter, reprises
his role as Carson, while she plays Maud,

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.059
one of Queen Mary's ladies-in-waiting.

00:05:02.059 --> 00:05:06.210
The movie premiered to positive reviews, and
it also allowed Staunton to reunite with her

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.280
Potter co-star Maggie Smith, who played Professor
McGonagall.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.480
"Are we going to kiss?"

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.360
"I'm glad you want to kiss me.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:16.680
It wasn't quite what you said when I last
heard from you."

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:17.920
"Something you'd like to say, dear?"

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.180
"Oh, there are several things I would like
to say."

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.580
The actress who played Dolores Umbridge isn't
just an acclaimed star of stage and screen.

00:05:25.589 --> 00:05:30.669
In 2006, Imelda Staunton made news when she
was named an Officer of the Order of the British

00:05:30.669 --> 00:05:31.160
Empire.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.580
Ten years later, she earned the title of Commander
of the British Empire, both thanks to her

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:36.809
work in the dramatic arts.

00:05:36.809 --> 00:05:40.749
Now, it seems that Staunton will take her
royal ambitions to the next level.

00:05:40.749 --> 00:05:45.210
According to Variety and the BBC, Staunton
will play the part of Queen Elizabeth in the

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.840
fifth and final season of The Crown.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.300
We can only be thankful that Dolores Umbridge
never achieved the power of the throne.

